# Gitleaks fingerprints — reviewed findings that are NOT secrets.
#
# Format: <commit>:<file>:<rule-id>:<line>. A fingerprint pins ONE finding at
# ONE coordinate in ONE commit. It is the narrowest suppression gitleaks has:
# unlike `paths` in .gitleaks.toml it exempts no file, no rule and no other
# line, so the same string anywhere else — including this file at a different
# line — is still a finding.
#
# INT-019. These three are the gitleaks self-test's own fixtures.
# gate_selftest.sh plants the two strings the .gitleaks.toml allowlist rows
# name, asserts they are accepted, then plants a real literal in the same two
# files and asserts those are rejected — the near-miss negative control that
# proves the rows are anchored to the captured secret and not to a path.
# Committing the fixtures as literals was the defect: it put a secret-shaped
# string in the generator, which the script's own header forbids. Commit
# 9fae031 removed them; the script now mirrors the lines out of the real files
# at run time, and HEAD is clean under both gitleaks 8.24.3 and 8.30.1.
#
# What survives is only the patch of the superseded commit. Nothing here was
# ever a credential, so there is nothing to rotate: INDEXER_PASSWORD is a
# compose-escaped variable reference resolved from OpenBao at run time
# (invariant 14), and WAF/CrowdSec is two product names in a prose sentence.
#
# These go inert when this PR squash-merges, because a68309d5 will not exist
# on main. They are kept only so the range scan on the PR itself is honest
# rather than silenced wholesale.
